This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   This session continued from a previous conversation that implemented a 1v1 real-time battle mode for a Phaser 3 "ddong avoid game." The user's requests in this session were:
   - Fix the countdown bug: "3이 뜨는데 게임 진행까지는 안가는데?" (3 shows but countdown doesn't progress)
   - Fix: "게임이 한쪽만 실행되는데? 아까 점수 다르다고 하기전까지는 게임은 실행이 됐었는데" (game only runs on one side)
   - Fix: "참가한 쪽만 게임이 실행된다고. 방 만든쪽은 시작을 안하고" (only joiner runs game, host doesn't start)
   - Fix: "방 만든쪽은 준비완료에서 멈춰있는데" (host stuck at "준비완료" screen)
   - Fix: "39 vs 39 인데 한쪽은 39 vs 36" (score discrepancy between screens)

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Phaser 3 scene lifecycle and TimerEvent management
   - Supabase Realtime Broadcast channel (singleton per topic name — `supabase.channel()` returns existing channel if same name exists)
   - `broadcast: { self: false }` works at WebSocket connection level, not userId level
   - Phaser `TimerEvent` does NOT have an `active` property like `GameObject` → must be tracked separately
   - `setInterval` vs Phaser `time.addEvent`: `setInterval` fires even in background tabs; Phaser timers require the game loop (rAF) to fire
   - State guard pattern with `countdownStarted` boolean flag
   - `uiGroup` bulk-destroy pattern for UI state management

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`src/scenes/BattleMatchScene.ts`** (primary file modified)
     - Added `countdownStarted: boolean = false` property to prevent double countdown
     - Added `readyRetryTimer: ReturnType<typeof setInterval> | null = null` for READY retry mechanism
     - Added `uiTimers: Phaser.Time.TimerEvent[] = []` for proper TimerEvent cleanup
     - Modified `clearUI()` to also call `timer.remove()` on all `uiTimers`
     - Modified `showCreateWaiting()` to use `this.uiTimers.push(...)` instead of casting timer to GameObject
     - Added `countdownStarted` reset in `handleCreateRoom()` and `doJoin()`
     - Modified `checkBothReady()` to check `!this.countdownStarted` guard
     - Modified `GAME_START` event handler to also check `!this.countdownStarted` guard
     - Modified `doSendReady()` to start `setInterval` retry of READY every 1500ms
     - Added `clearReadyRetry()` helper method
     - Changed `goToBattle()` from async (await destroy) to sync using `destroyImmediate()`
     - Added `clearReadyRetry()` calls in `goToBattle()`, `goBack()`, and `shutdown()`

     Key current state of critical methods:
     ```typescript
     private countdownStarted: boolean = false;
     private readyRetryTimer: ReturnType<typeof setInterval> | null = null;
     private uiTimers: Phaser.Time.TimerEvent[] = [];

     private clearUI() {
       this.removeInput();
       for (const obj of this.uiGroup) {
         if (obj.active) obj.destroy();
       }
       this.uiGroup = [];
       for (const timer of this.uiTimers) {
         timer.remove();
       }
       this.uiTimers = [];
     }

     private checkBothReady() {
       if (this.myReady && this.opponentReady && this.isHost && !this.countdownStarted) {
         this.countdownStarted = true;
         this.battleChannel?.sendGameStart(Date.now());
         this.showCountdown();
       }
     }

     // In setupChannelListeners():
     this.battleChannel.onEvent(BattleEvent.GAME_START, () => {
       if (!this.countdownStarted) {
         this.countdownStarted = true;
         this.showCountdown();
       }
     });

     private doSendReady() {
       if (!this.battleChannel || this.myReady) return;
       this.myReady = true;
       const charId = getSafeSelectedCharacter();
       this.battleChannel.sendReady(charId);
       this.clearUI();
       // ... show UI ...
       this.clearReadyRetry();
       this.readyRetryTimer = setInterval(() => {
         if (this.countdownStarted || !this.battleChannel) {
           this.clearReadyRetry();
           return;
         }
         this.battleChannel.sendReady(charId);
       }, 1500);
       this.checkBothReady();
     }

     private goToBattle() {
       this.clearReadyRetry();
       const roomCode = this.battleChannel?.code ?? '';
       const userId = this.userId;
       if (this.battleChannel) {
         this.battleChannel.destroyImmediate();
         this.battleChannel = null;
       }
       this.scene.start('BattleGameScene', { roomCode, userId });
     }

     // showCreateWaiting dots timer (fixed):
     this.uiTimers.push(
       this.time.addEvent({
         delay: 500,
         loop: true,
         callback: () => {
           dotCount = (dotCount + 1) % 4;
           if (dots.active) dots.setText('대기 중' + '.'.repeat(dotCount));
         },
       })
     );
     ```

   - **`src/utils/battleChannel.ts`** (modified)
     - Added `destroyImmediate()` synchronous method that calls `supabase.removeChannel()` without awaiting `untrack()`
     - This is needed because `supabase.channel()` is a singleton — it returns an existing channel by same topic name. Must remove before BattleGameScene creates a new one with the same name.
     ```typescript
     destroyImmediate(): void {
       if (this.channel) {
         supabase.removeChannel(this.channel);
         this.channel = null;
       }
     }
     ```

   - **`src/scenes/BattleGameScene.ts`** (modified)
     - Added final `sendScoreUpdate(this.score)` in the GAME_OVER handler before calling `endBattle(WIN)`, so the loser receives the winner's most current score
     ```typescript
     this.battleChannel.onEvent(BattleEvent.GAME_OVER, (payload) => {
       if (!this.battleFinished) {
         this.opponentScore = payload.finalScore;
         // Send final score to loser before ending
         if (this.channelReady && this.battleChannel) {
           this.battleChannel.sendScoreUpdate(this.score);
         }
         this.endBattle(BattleResult.WIN);
       }
     });
     ```

4. Errors and Fixes:
   - **Countdown freezes at "3"**: `checkBothReady()` called twice from READY handler (once inside `doSendReady()`, once at end of handler). Second `showCountdown()` call's `clearUI()` destroyed the first call's `countText`. Fix: `countdownStarted` guard flag in `checkBothReady()`.
   - **Only one side starts game (singleton channel bug)**: Verified via Supabase source code (`node_modules/@supabase/realtime-js/dist/module/RealtimeClient.js` line 276) that `supabase.channel()` returns existing channel if same topic exists. Fire-and-forget async `destroy()` meant `removeChannel()` hadn't run when BattleGameScene tried to create new channel — got stale channel. Fix: `destroyImmediate()` synchronous method.
   - **Host stuck at "준비완료" / `drawImage on null` crash**: Dots animation `TimerEvent` in `showCreateWaiting()` was stored in `uiGroup` via `as unknown as Phaser.GameObjects.GameObject`. Since `TimerEvent` has no `active` property, `clearUI()`'s `if (obj.active) obj.destroy()` skipped it. Timer kept firing → called `setText()` on destroyed `dots` text → Phaser crash → host scene broken. Fix: Added separate `uiTimers` array with `timer.remove()` in `clearUI()`.
   - **Score discrepancy (39 vs 39 on one side, 39 vs 36 on other)**: Winner stopped sending score updates immediately after receiving GAME_OVER. Loser displayed the last received score before death (slightly stale). Fix: Winner sends one final `sendScoreUpdate(this.score)` in GAME_OVER handler before transitioning.

5. Problem Solving:
   - Identified that Supabase `channel()` is singleton by inspecting `node_modules/@supabase/realtime-js/dist/module/RealtimeClient.js`
   - Discovered `broadcast: { self: false }` is connection-based, not userId-based — confirmed via Supabase source
   - Identified `TimerEvent` vs `GameObject` casting issue as true root cause of host crash
   - Score sync issue solved by sending final score update when GAME_OVER is received

